<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>

  <!-- Vanilla Textures Expanded (VanillaExpanded.VTEXE) compat: match the unique spear's held pose
       and apparent length to VTE's redrawn vanilla spear.

       Why: VTE redraws Core's Spear.png from a horizontal, tip-right sprite (which our five
       UniqueSpear* variants deliberately match) into a corner-to-corner diagonal, tip top-right -
       the ONLY melee texture it reorients (its Longsword/Knife/etc. stay horizontal). It ships no
       compensating XML or C# (verified against workshop item 2016436324 v1.6: its patches touch
       shuttles/animals/plants/main buttons only; MeleeWeapon_Spear appears nowhere), so with VTE on
       a drafted vanilla spear renders 45 degrees off ours and ~1.37x longer. Reported on the
       Workshop as our spear looking wrong while drafted (2026-08).

       Both fixes are def-side, so this is XML rather than 10 extra textures (5 variants + masks)
       that VTE-less players would download for nothing:

       - equippedAngleOffset: PawnRenderUtility.DrawEquipmentAiming rotates the sprite by
         (aimAngle - 90 + equippedAngleOffset), clockwise-positive (Unity AngleAxis about +Y). The
         base spear ships -25; VTE's art bakes in a further 45 degrees COUNTER-clockwise (tip
         top-right), so emulating it on our horizontal art is -25 - 45 = -70. The west-facing branch
         mirrors the mesh and SUBTRACTS the offset, so a single value serves both facings.
       - drawSize: 1.6's DrawEquipmentAiming scales the held mesh by Graphic.drawSize (older
         versions drew a fixed 1x1 plane), and Graphic_Random passes drawSize to every variant.
         Measured opaque extents (alpha > 40): VTE Spear.png spans 1.370 cells corner to corner
         with a 0.088-cell shaft; UniqueSpearA/C/E span 1.00-1.01 cells with a 0.078-0.086 shaft.
         1.35 would match the length to within 2% but thickens our shaft to ~0.115 cells; 1.3
         (length 1.30, shaft ~0.11) was chosen by eye as the better balance against VTE's thinner
         shaft - the accepted trade for no new art. Tune here if VTE's art changes.
       - modExtensions/CarriedWeaponOffsetExtension (our C#, see its header): where a drafted idle
         pawn grips the sprite. Our head is longer than VTE's (~0.44 vs ~0.29 cells at 1.3x), so
         with the default grip at texture centre the spear reads as held near the tip when facing
         north or south; east/west read fine. Shifting the sprite along the shaft toward the tip
         (held angle 143 - 90 - 70 = -17 degrees, i.e. mostly right, a little up) moves the grip
         toward the butt. Vanilla offers no XML hook for the carried pose, hence the extension.
       - uiIconScale: GenUI.IconDrawScale multiplies the UI icon by min(drawSize / Size), so the
         drawSize bump would enlarge and crop the inventory/trade icon. 1 / 1.3 cancels it.

       Gated by the load root (LoadFolders.xml, IfModActive on VTE's packageId) rather than
       PatchOperationFindMod, which matches by display NAME and breaks on a rename; and, inside
       that, by the matchVteSpear setting (default on) for players whose texture stack puts the
       vanilla spear back to horizontal after VTE, or who simply want the shipped look. This root
       holds Patches only; the StageMod manifest must glob <version>/Mods/*/Patches/** or it
       deploys nothing and fails silently in-game. -->

  <!-- The whole compat is switchable: PatchOperation_UMWSetting (our C#, header there) reads the
       matchVteSpear setting at patch time, so with it off the def keeps its shipped values, carries
       no extension, and the render patch never applies. Settings_Compat.cs owns the row. -->
  <Operation Class="UniqueMeleeWeapons.PatchOperation_UMWSetting">
    <setting>matchVteSpear</setting>
    <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
      <operations>
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="UMW_Spear_Unique"]</xpath>
          <value>
            <equippedAngleOffset>-70</equippedAngleOffset>
            <uiIconScale>0.77</uiIconScale>
            <modExtensions>
              <li Class="UniqueMeleeWeapons.CarriedWeaponOffsetExtension">
                <north>(0.07, 0, 0.04)</north>
                <south>(0.07, 0, 0.04)</south>
              </li>
            </modExtensions>
          </value>
        </li>

        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="UMW_Spear_Unique"]/graphicData</xpath>
          <value>
            <drawSize>1.3</drawSize>
          </value>
        </li>
      </operations>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
